I had similar experiences when I ascended a Barbarian who had -34 AC and
a +6 Vorpal Blade.  The problem was on the fire level.  I got a couple
of Archons next to me, and they kept blinding and stunning me.  Of
course, I had lost my telepathy and never managed to get it back, so I
couldn't tell where the Archons were attacking me from.  The stun
usually went away before I got to move, so I would get to apply my
unicorn horn once to rid myself of blindness, then I would get one
attack on an Archon (thanks to the "very fast" intrinsic).  This is a
losing game with an Archon, though, especially since they appeared to
keep summoning more, as well as other assorted nasties.  I ended up
praying once and burning two amulets of life saving (I had six more in
the pack though, all gotten without polypiling, so I was okay, but it
was obnoxious).  Archons are definately the nastiest creature in the
game...but that's okay with me.  There should be some creature capable
of killing a ~350 hp barbarian...lord knows the Wizard doesn't have a
prayer.

